WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.340
Episode 6

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.340
Space Destroyer Yukikaze
Rests on a Field of Ice!

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.340
( Air date: Nov 11, 1974 )

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:42.220
Space Battleship

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:42.220
<i>YAMATO</i>

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:40.810
In 2199, Earth was attacked by the
mysterious planet, Gamilus...

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:47.540
{YUUSEI}...and mankind was facing extinction due to the
poisons from the meteor bombs in one year.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.990
{KONO}A device to purify the
poisons is on Iscandar...

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:54.730
{KONO}...which is 148,000 light years away
in the large Magellanic Cloud.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:02:01.770
{CHIKYUU}The space battleship Yamato is the only
ship which can exceed the speed of light...

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:07.580
{OUFUKU}...and it has just departed on a
round trip of 296,000 light years.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.990
{YAMATO}The Yamato also carried out a
test firing of its primary weapon...

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.050
{YAMATO}...the Wave Motion gun,
at Jupiter.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:14.940
What ?
A Wave Motion gun ?

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:19.200
Yes.  I've never seen such
a powerful cannon before.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:26.330
We have to react quickly, or the
Yamato will become a great threat.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:29.390
Vice President Hisu

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.400
A Wave Motion gun
on an Earth ship ?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.190
Please, inform our Lord.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.510
Pluto Frontline Base Commander, Shultz

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.460
Wait for a moment.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:44.940
That Yamato.  Soon, you'll see how
strong our Lord Desler's Gamilus is.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.960
I'll tell you
Lord Desler's words.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.470
He only wants to hear about your
victory announcement.  Understood ?

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.180
Vice President Hisu...

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:04.800
I understand. I'll report to you
with a victory no matter the risk.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:08.370
No matter what...Yamato.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.640
Engine room,
investigate the cause.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.440
The energy transfer
pipe has overheated.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.760
Say what ?
Overheated ?!

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.070
It must be because of the shock
of the Wave Motion gun test.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:52.330
Precisely. The Yamato doesn't have the
space alloy, Cosmonite, onboard.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.950
Can we find it somewhere ?

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.990
I heard that Titan,
a moon of Saturn, has it.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:00.490
Mori, analyze
Titan immediately.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:01.550
Aye, sir.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.740
Ouch.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.240
What's Shima doing ?

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.400
Hey, are you trying
to wreck the Yamato ?

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.140
What're you talking about, Kodai ?

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.140
The problem was caused by the
shock of the Wave Motion gun test.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:27.790
Really ?

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.760
Analysis of
Titan is complete.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.370
An optical analysis shows that
there's a small amount of Cosmonite.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.490
Shima, ahead slow.
 We'll head for Titan.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.090
The engine will overheat.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.690
The Yamato needs the Cosmonite.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.690
Aye.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:11.590
Saturn.  This unique
and beautiful planet...

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:14.470
Saturn

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:15.690
...is the second largest planet in
the solar system, next to Jupiter.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:20.760
{chokkei}Its 115,000 km diameter is
nine times of the Earth's.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:25.540
{HOTONDO}It's mostly covered with a cloud of
methane, and the interior is unknown.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:29.210
{BOUSHI}Its ring looks like the brim of a
hat, made of rock and ice...

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.740
{YUKKURI}...and is slowly
rotating around Saturn.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:40.730
{DOSEI}Saturn has nine moons, and Titan
is said to have air just like Earth.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:44.780
{TADASHI}Temperature is very low, due
to the distance from the sun...

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:47.290
A moon of Saturn, Titan

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:49.650
{OOKUNO}...but it's assumed that
there are many metal elements.

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:02.890
It stopped near Titan.
Gantz, run an analysis.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:09.490
Energy is extremely low.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:12.240
What ?  Energy is
extremely low ?

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.040
It could have malfunctioned.
We'll send a fleet immediately and...

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:18.250
Wait, don't
act carelessly.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.610
I'll split you in two teams.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:31.040
Mori and Analyzer will search for
the Cosmonite with Kodai as guard.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.000
Aye, sir.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:37.080
Mr. Sanada, you'll form your own team,
and collect materials from Titan.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:37.890
Aye, sir.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.690
Listen carefully.
The Yamato isn't in good shape.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:45.930
We can't let the enemy know
our reasons for staying here.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:50.020
So act quickly but
be cautious. That's all.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:50.830
Aye, sir.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.680
Alright, we'll
have a race, Kodai.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.200
You're on.{Why not.}

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.490
Don't play around.
This isn't a field trip.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:29.440
But...

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.540
It's a job.
Let's be serious.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.240
A patrol and
transports have launched.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:42.340
What're they going
to do on Titan ?

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:43.730
Let's investigate.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.440
To the patrol ship near Titan...
To the patrol ship near Titan...

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:54.550
This is Yaretana of the Gamilus patrol
ship 104, cruising near Saturn moon No. 6.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:59.730
The Yamato is near Titan, and it has
sent a few small boats to the surface.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:01.720
Investigate their objectives.
That's all.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:02.520
Roger.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:21.530
So beautiful.  There isn't such
beautiful scenery on Earth anymore.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:24.790
Analyzer, is there any
sign of the Cosmonite?

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.960
Please, fly a little longer.
I'll run a triangulation search.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.790
Shima, Aihara, pay close
attention to the surroundings.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.450
We don't know when
the enemy will appear.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.430
Aye, sir.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:18.780
Hurry, we don't
have much time.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.190
What was that ?

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.350
A shooting star ?

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:30.780
An unidentified object
detected behind Titan.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:34.990
It's not a shooting star.
It's assumed to be a Gamilus patrol.

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:36.690
Warn all
deployed personnel.

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:40.510
To Mori and Sanada teams, an
unidentified object was detected.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.480
Finish quickly.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:44.290
Stay alert and
finish your tasks soon.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.810
Okay. Abort your work
and return to the Yamato.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:11.520
Kodai, what's wrong ?
Hurry up.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.210
Analyzer, anything yet ?
You useless piece of junk.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.120
Don't say that.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.120
Not yet.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.330
Okay, let's turn right.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:26.990
It's dangerous.
Return to the ship immediately.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:28.940
I'm concerned about
that UFO a while ago.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.540
Analyzer.

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:36.620
A reaction, left 35 degrees,
distance 3 miles.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.500
I see.
Alright, let's go.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.780
But Kodai, what about
the return order ?

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.590
This is Kodai.
We've found Cosmonite.

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:48.470
We'll begin mining
immediately. Over.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:50.610
Kodai, please
return immediately.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.990
Kodai. Kodai.  Kodai !

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:58.100
Captain, Kodai turned
off his communicator.

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.430
That's it.

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:24.220
That's Cosmonite...

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:36.330
In any case,
let's mine this quickly.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.670
Analyzer, hurry up.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:39.570
If it's for you...

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.980
This looks like a mining site.
It has cutter marks.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.920
They're mining Cosmonite.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.090
What ?
They're mining Cosmonite ?

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:38.550
I see.  Cosmonite is a space alloy
that's used for energy transfer conduits.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:41.050
The Yamato must
have been damaged.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.690
Interfere with their
mining activities.

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:44.550
Aye, sir.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.940
By the way,
how many are they ?

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:49.090
One male, one female
and one robot.

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:52.640
Great. They'll be great samples to
study our enemy.  Capture them.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:53.000
Aye, sir.

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.160
Unknown vehicles
are approaching.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.000
Say what ?

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.520
Space tanks ?

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:16.760
Radar signal is gone.
Something must have happened.

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:17.600
Bearing ?

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.150
Run behind that
rock over there !

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.310
Don't miss.  But make sure
you only injure them.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.070
Dammit.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:39.320
That's why I warned you.
We should have returned quickly.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.870
Shut up.
You protect Mori.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:50.370
Fool.  Do you think you can destroy
a space tank with a cosmo gun ?

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:58.890
We're doomed at this rate.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.910
You aim at the guy
behind the rocks.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.130
I'll capture the
woman and the robot.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:35.550
Don't blame me.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.160
Run !
It's dangerous !

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:01.120
Hurry.

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:23.200
Watch out !

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.230
W...what the
hell is that ?

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:53.280
Analyzer.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:54.850
You're awesome.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.150
If it's for Miss Mori.

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:09.700
Tsuba kukansa ruma

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:13.590
Translated, "Everyone,
get in the tank over there."

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:19.610
Ruma kukansa tsuba.

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:20.610
Dammit.

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:28.870
Captain, an SOS !
It's from Analyzer !

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:33.000
Tsuba ruma da kansatsu

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.430
It's gone.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.850
We've got its origin.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:48.420
X35 degrees, Y30 degrees,
Z65 degrees on Titan.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:56.250
Tsuba ruma

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.500
Cosmo gun...

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:02.170
It's risky.

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:05.650
No, I'll try.
Analyzer, guard Mori.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:29.650
How come it was here ?
Whose cosmo gun is this ?

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.530
Kodai
Mamoru

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:38.760
Mamoru... My brother's name...
My brother's cosmo gun !

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.370
YU

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:44.290
KI

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:45.040
KA

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:45.790
ZE

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:49.040
YUKIKAZE

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:51.040
My brother's ship !
My brother's...

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:10.080
My brother's...
My brother's Yukikaze !

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:11.870
Brother !

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:24.100
Brother !

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:27.100
Brother !

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.380
Aren't you here, Brother ?!

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.410
Captain, Kodai's
ship isn't following.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:44.670
Not following ?!

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:53.940
Okita, I can't run away.
Please, let me go.

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.940
Good luck, and please
take care of Earth.

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:06.150
Don't die, Kodai.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:36.510
Kodai...

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.810
Kodai, let's go.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.140
Brother, I'll avenge you.

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:52.790
All systems on line.{All ship releived}

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:56.500
The repairs on the energy transfer pipe are finished, thanks to the Cosmonite.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.970
Shima, standard
ship settings.{normalize the ship.}

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:00.760
Aye, sir.

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:16.800
Engine, nominal.

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.390
Setting cruise speed.

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:28.620
Excellent, Shima.

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.790
I owe it to Mr. Sanada.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.850
No, it was Mori's work.

00:21:33.110 --> 00:21:35.300
No, it was my work.

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:39.650
Bring the Yamato back
on course.  Ahead full.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:40.390
Aye, sir.

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:42.920
When Kodai returns,
send him to my quarters.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.990
He's upset at
Kodai's disobedience.

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:51.050
But we were able to find
the Cosmonite, thanks to him.

00:21:51.050 --> 00:21:52.270
That's true.

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:55.110
Oh, aren't you hurt ?

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:57.830
Thanks for the Cosmonite.

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:00.880
We were able to get it,
because Kodai protected us.

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:04.190
But Kodai, the Captain
wants to see you.

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:07.190
Kodai, it might be
about your disobedience.

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:09.150
Okay, I'll go.

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:26.170
Kodai Susumu, reporting.

00:22:29.590 --> 00:22:32.070
Report about the Yukikaze.

00:22:32.070 --> 00:22:33.740
Y...yes, sir.

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:39.480
The destroyer Yukikaze of the Earth fleet
seems to have crash-landed on Titan...

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:42.540
...and there were
no survivors.

00:22:46.670 --> 00:22:48.740
No survivors, huh...?

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:55.480
Kodai...

00:22:55.480 --> 00:22:56.290
Sir ?

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:01.780
We don't want the Earth to
be like the Yukikaze, do we ?

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:02.800
No, sir.

00:23:10.090 --> 00:23:14.870
The Yamato was repaired with the
Cosmonite, and it departed Saturn.

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:17.760
{CHIKYUU}It has been five days
since it left Earth.

00:23:17.760 --> 00:23:23.590
{CHIKYUU}The people on Earth are suffering
from the radioactive poison of Gamilus.

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:27.700
{ISOGE}Yamato, begin your journey
of 296,000 light years soon.

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:32.490
{JINRUI}There's only 359 days left
till the extinction of mankind.

00:23:31.780 --> 00:23:38.170
359 days left till the Destruction of Earth

00:23:33.230 --> 00:23:38.070
{JINRUI}There's only 359 days left
till the extinction of mankind.

00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:46.100
Okita Juzo:

00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:46.100
Naya Goro

00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:52.100
Sanada Shiro:

00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:52.100
Aono Takeshi

00:23:59.140 --> 00:24:08.640
Note:
An ex-Mushi Production, Yoshikazu Yasuhiko joined as a storyboard drawer.  He worked on 13 episodes in the first TV series.

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:18.640
Note:
The Destroyer Yukikaze was sunk at Pluto, but found on Saturn, which is 5.4 million km away.  The Yukikaze must have been seized by Gamilus, and the ship must have been left on Titan.

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:28.640
Note:
Gamilus scout commander Yaretara speaks Gamilus, "ruma kukan satsuba," in front of Kodai.  It reads circle, triangle, x in reverse.  It was made up at the recording studio.

00:24:28.640 --> 00:24:34.590
Note:
The voice of Shultz in this episode was done by Kazuo Kato.

00:24:35.170 --> 00:24:41.760
Translation

00:24:35.170 --> 00:24:41.760
Editing

00:24:41.760 --> 00:24:49.340
Timing

00:24:41.760 --> 00:24:49.340
Song Translations

00:24:49.340 --> 00:24:54.290
A
